    "id": 4,
    "title": "Midnight at Hollow House",
    "author": "Riley Quinn",
    "genre": "Horror",
    "cover": "images/cover-art-04.jpg",
    "scene": "images/scene-04.svg",
    "synopsis": "Three friends spend a stormy night in an abandoned house and learn the unsettling truth behind its lights.",
    "chapter": "The Light Upstairs",
    "story": "The first light appeared in Hollow House at 11:53 p.m., though the electricity had been disconnected for years. From the road, Nina saw it flicker in an upstairs window. Her friends Paolo and Tess said it was probably a reflection, but neither of them could explain why the light moved from room to room.\n\nThey had come to the house to film a short documentary about the town’s oldest rumor. People said the former owner, Dr. Vale, had disappeared during a storm and that anyone who saw the upstairs light would hear a voice calling their name. Nina did not believe in ghosts. She believed in good footage, and the glowing window was too perfect to ignore.\n\nInside, the house smelled of wet wood and dust. Their flashlights revealed family portraits, a staircase, and a hallway where the wallpaper had peeled into long strips. When the upstairs light appeared again, it shone through the floorboards directly above them. Then came three slow knocks.\n\nTess wanted to leave. Paolo, trying to sound brave, called out, “Who’s there?” A voice answered from the ceiling: “The door is still open.” The words were clear enough that Nina stopped recording. They followed the sound to a locked room at the end of the hall. The key was hidden beneath a loose stair, as if someone had left it for them.\n\nInside, they found no ghost, only an old radio, a lamp powered by a small generator, and dozens of notebooks. The notebooks belonged to Dr. Vale’s daughter, Clara, who had been confined to the room during a long illness because the family feared the town would gossip. The radio was connected to a timer, and the voice they heard was an old recording. But why had it been running?\n\nA final notebook explained that Clara had escaped the house during the storm and survived, leaving the recordings behind so someone would discover what had happened. Dr. Vale had told the town she died, then abandoned the property after the truth began to spread. The upstairs light was part of a simple signal system Clara had built to guide herself through the house when she could not sleep.\n\nAs they searched the desk, the generator sputtered. The lamp went out, and the recording stopped halfway through a sentence. In the silence, Nina heard real rain tapping the window and realized how easily fear had turned a sad history into a monster story. They called the local historian from the porch and waited outside until help arrived.\n\nThe next morning, the historian confirmed that Clara had lived in another town under her mother’s name. Nina’s documentary became a story about a girl whose voice had been ignored, not a haunted house. She left the last shot on the dark upstairs window, then turned the camera toward the sun rising behind it.\n\nHollow House still creaked in the wind. But after that night, nobody in their town called the light a curse. They called it a message that had finally been heard.",
